{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation complete in worktree retire-review-316a (branch retire-review-316a), pending Gerrit.\n\nRED-first: authored tests/unit/test_cli_review_alias.py (22 tests) and confirmed all 18 behavioural cases RED before any source change. Held the edge/E2E cases out of the implementer subagent's tree; it saw only the 8 happy-path cases. Full oracle restored and validated GREEN afterwards.\n\nTeeth check: three mutations each caught a held-out test — (1) dropping the forwarded --no-sign fails test_shim_forwards_no_sign; (2) disabling the --graph rejection and (3) disabling the positional-reviewer rejection each fail test_rejections_happen_before_any_llm_call.\n\nOne correction applied post-handoff: the implementer duplicated _review_plan's body inside the shim. Rewrote it to DELEGATE by forwarding argv to _review_plan(...) as the plan specifies, so the shim inherits the target verb's exit codes/rendering/error handling instead of drifting from a copied body. Full oracle stayed green.\n\nOne test-defect fix under revert-first discipline: test_non_claimable_fast_fails needed --source local because the tmp fixture repo has no commits, so the default attested snapshot cannot resolve a ref (orthogonal to the fast-fail being pinned). Re-confirmed RED for the right reason against un-implemented code first: the old verb reached the model (provider 401) instead of fast-failing.\n\nGates local: make lint PASS, make typecheck PASS (432 files), scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py exit 0, module-size max in src/rebar unchanged at 800 (cap) with _llm_commands.py at 758 (was 742).\n\nNamed regression suites all green, including the fourteen unedited direct callers of the public op, which now record a DeprecationWarning rather than raising it (pytest has no filterwarnings key) - that is the in-session proof the impl split is behaviour-preserving.\n\nAlso regenerated docs/mcp-reference.md via scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py after tightening the tool docstring's first line, so the generated row keeps its payload description."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785900161942932001,"uuid":"454b00d3-1152-4214-b5ba-595ce286071f"}